'''Volisanian Balboa Airlines''' ({{lang|ca|Aerolínies Volisanianes de Balboa}}) was a subsidiary of [[Volisanian Airlines]] that operated in the [[Balboa|Republic of Balboa]] during the period preceding and encompassing the [[Great Adonian War]]. The airline was established as a subsidiary of the Volisanian flag carrier to serve the rump Balboan state that had been reduced to its post-[[Treaty of Sant Llàtzer|Sant Llàtzer]] borders following the [[Second War of the Isthmus]]. It operated from [[Sant Bart]], the capital of the rump republic, providing domestic services within Balboan territory and international connections to [[Volisania]].

The airline's operations were shaped by the political alignment of the Balboan state with Volisania during the interwar period. After the [[National Volisan Party]] seized power in Volisania in 1911 and the Balboan government adopted a fascist administration aligned with Volisania, the airline served as the principal air link between the two countries. During the [[Great Adonian War]], the airline supported the Volisan and Balboan war effort on the isthmus, operating from Sant Bart in support of the [[Balboa Campaign]] against [[Zong Balboa]]. The airline's surviving assets were merged into [[Aeroístmus]] in 1948 alongside those of [[Zong Balboa Airways]].

== History ==

Volisanian Balboa Airlines was established in 1934 as a subsidiary of [[Volisanian Airlines]], the Volisanian flag carrier. The airline was created to serve the rump Balboan state that had existed since the [[Treaty of Sant Llàtzer]] (1899), which had reduced Balboa to its southern territories following the loss of Sant Cristòfor and the canal zone to [[Zong]]. The airline's operational base was at [[Sant Bart]], which served as the capital of the rump republic.

The airline's establishment reflected the close political and economic relationship between Balboa and Volisania during the interwar period. After the [[National Volisan Party]] came to power in Volisania in 1911, the Balboan government under the [[Balboa Independence Party]] adopted a fascist administration aligned with Volisania. Both states shared a commitment to the reconquest of Sant Cristòfor and the canal, and the airline served as a commercial and logistical link between the two allies.

The airline operated domestic services within Balboan territory, connecting Sant Bart with the outlying communities of the rump state, and international services to Volisania, principally to [[Ampuria]]. The {{w|Douglas DC-3}} was among the aircraft types operated.

=== Great Adonian War ===

The [[Great Adonian War]] opened in 1935 with the [[Balboa Campaign]], a coordinated assault by Volisan and Balboan forces against [[Zong Balboa]]. The campaign aimed to seize Sant Cristòfor and the canal before Zong could reinforce its garrison. Volisanian Balboa Airlines supported the war effort, operating from Sant Bart in support of the military campaign.

The campaign succeeded in seizing the canal zone in its opening weeks but failed to capture Sant Cristòfor, which was defended by its walls and sustained by Zong naval supply lines. The resulting siege persisted for the duration of the war. During this period, the airline operated from Sant Bart, providing logistical support to the Volisan and Balboan forces besieging the city and maintaining domestic services within the Balboan-controlled territory.

The airline's operations were disrupted by the eventual collapse of the Volisan fascist government in 1947, which brought the war to an end. The cessation of hostilities left the airline in a diminished state, with reduced capacity and a route network disrupted by the conflict.

=== Dissolution ===

In 1948, the [[Adonian Community]] assumed responsibility for the post-war administration of the isthmus. The surviving assets of Volisanian Balboa Airlines were merged with those of [[Zong Balboa Airways]] to form [[Aeroístmus]], a new carrier managed by an AC consortium comprising representatives of the AC, the Balboan provisional authority, and the former Zong Balboa and Volisanian Balboa airline administrations. The merger ended the separate corporate existence of Volisanian Balboa Airlines.

